                <pb facs="0395" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg335"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Campbell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic">October 11,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 17, of August 21, in which you relate the arrangements made for
                    the return of Mrs. Waller and her family to Paris.</p>
                <p>Your course throughout in this matter meets with the approval of the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Second Assistant Secretary</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
